# Python virtual environments (e.g. the uv-managed IsaacLab venv, and the small
# Isaac-free downstream env built by transfer/setup_venv.sh).
# No trailing slash: a git worktree SYMLINKS the venv rather than copying it, and a
# "name/" pattern matches only a real directory -- so the symlink was not ignored and
# `git add -A` staged it. `/clips`, `/hf` and `/logs` already use this form.
/env_isaaclab
/env_transfer
*.venv/

# Isaac-Sim packman
_isaac_sim*
_repo
_build
.lastformat

# RL-Games
**/runs/*
**/logs/*
**/recordings/*

# The `**/logs/*` rule above ignores a logs directory's CONTENTS, which misses the root
# `logs` SYMLINK used in git worktrees (git does not descend into it).  No trailing slash,
# for the same reason as `/clips` below.
/logs

# Pre-Trained Checkpoints
/.pretrained_checkpoints/

# Teleop Recorded Dataset
datasets

transfer/obelisk/install/
transfer/obelisk/log/
transfer/obelisk/build/
# Policy pairs pulled from HuggingFace by prefetch_policy.py (~130 MB per pair)
transfer/obelisk/g1_control/resource/hf_cache/
# Debug clip libraries: a deployment artifact like the ONNX pair, generated by
# scripts/rsl_rl/make_debug_clips.py. Lives inside the package because the container
# mounts only $REPO_ROOT and the robot has no clips/ directory.
transfer/obelisk/g1_control/resource/debug_clips/
transfer/obelisk/docker/.env
# The Jetson ZED container's env, same reasoning: per-box (ZED_IMAGE has to name the SDK
# installed on THAT host), and .env_example is what is tracked.
transfer/jetson/zed/docker/.env
# The ZED box's own Cyclone config: it names THIS box's interface address, so committing it
# would hand every box one machine's addressing. config/cyclonedds.xml.example is tracked.
transfer/jetson/zed/config/cyclonedds.xml
# One machine's view of the split link: its own interface address and the OTHER box as a
# peer. Committing it would hand every box the desktop's half of an asymmetric pair, which
# is the "one box sees the other's topics and not the reverse" failure the example warns
# about. Same reasoning as .env above; docker/cyclonedds.xml.example is what is tracked.
transfer/obelisk/docker/cyclonedds.xml
# The staged copy of ANOTHER box's half of the same asymmetric pair (the Thor's, for the
# split-sim brain). It is one machine's view for exactly the reason above, and it does
# nothing where it sits -- it is written here, copied to that box, and pointed at by that
# box's CYCLONEDDS_URI.
transfer/obelisk/docker/cyclonedds.*.xml
